## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

| Severity | Count |
|----------|-------|
| **Critical** | 2 (systemic — affects all 10 tests) |
| **Medium** | 2 |
| **Low** | 1 |

This suite is the textbook definition of **coverage-touching**: every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called exactly once, in declaration order, with zero or near-zero verification. You hit 95% coverage because every line *executes* — but no test would fail if any method returned wrong data, mutated the wrong record, or silently dropped input.

---

### 🔴 Critical

#### 1. No Assertions (6 of 10 tests)

These tests call a method and discard the result. They will pass even if the method is a no-op.

| Test (line) | What's called | What's asserted |
|---|---|---|
| `AddProduct_Works` (17) | `AddProduct()` | Nothing |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` (32) | `UpdatePrice()` | Nothing |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` (38) | `RemoveProduct()` | Nothing |
| `GetProductCount_Works` (63) | `GetProductCount()` | Nothing |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (68) | `ApplyBulkDiscount()` | Nothing |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` (85) | `ImportFromCsv()` | Nothing |

**Fix — `AddProduct_Works` (example, same pattern for all):**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_StoresProductRetrievableBySku()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);

    var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved?.Name);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved?.Price);
}
```

**Fix — `UpdatePrice_Works`:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void UpdatePrice_ChangesStoredPrice()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);

    var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated?.Price);
}
```

**Fix — `RemoveProduct_Works`:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void RemoveProduct_MakesProductUnretrievable()
{
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    _catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");

    Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
}
```

**Fix — `GetProductCount_Works`:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetProductCount_ReturnsNumberOfStoredProducts()
{
    Assert.AreEqual(0, _catalog.GetProductCount());
    _catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
    Assert.AreEqual(1, _catalog.GetProductCount());
